paragraph.content:
Check the expiration date on the carton (see 
                           Figure C
                        ).

list.item:
Do not use the medicine if the expiration date has passed. If the expiration date has passed, safely throw away (dispose of) the carton in an FDA-cleared sharps disposal container (see 
   Step 20. Throw away (dispose of) STEQEYMA
).

Leave the carton containing the STEQEYMA vial at room temperature 68°F to 77°F (20°C to 25°C) for 30 minutes to allow it to warm up (see 
                           Figure D
                        ).

Wash your hands with soap and water and dry them thoroughly (see 
                           Figure E
                        ).

Check the expiration date on the label of the vial (see 
                           Figure F
                        ).

Look at the medicine in the vial to make sure that the liquid is clear to very slightly opalescent and colorless to pale yellow (see 
                           Figure G
                        ).

Clean the skin with an alcohol wipe where you plan to give the injection (see 
                           Figure I
                        ).

Remove the protective cap from the STEQEYMA vial. Throw away the cap (see 
                           Figure J
                        ).

Wipe the rubber stopper of the vial with an alcohol wipe and allow it to dry (see 
                           Figure K
                        ).

Hold the syringe at the middle of the syringe body with the needle pointing away from yourself, and pull the needle cap straight off the syringe (see 
                           Figure L
                        ).

Throw away (dispose of) the needle cap right away in an FDA-cleared sharps disposal container (see 
                           Step 20. Throw away (dispose of) STEQEYMA
                        ).

With your other hand, pull on the plunger rod to fill the syringe with the amount of medicine prescribed by the healthcare provider (see 
                           Figure N
                        ).

If there are air bubbles, gently tap the side of the syringe until the air bubbles go to the top of the syringe (see 
                           Figure O
                        ).

Hold the body of the syringe in one hand between the thumb and index fingers (see 
                           Figure P
                        ).

Use a quick and dart-like motion to insert the needle into the pinched skin at about a 45-degree angle (see 
                           Figure P
                        ).

Make sure you have injected all of the STEQEYMA medicine (see 
                           Figure Q
                        ).

After the syringe is empty, release the pinched skin and slowly pull the needle out of the injection site. (see 
                           Figure R
                        ).

There may be some bleeding at the injection site. This is normal (see 
                           Step 18. Care for the injection site
                        ).

Put the used needle, syringe and vial in an FDA-cleared sharps disposal container right away after use (see 
                           Figure S
                        ).

text.paragraph:
STEQEYMA prefilled syringes are available in 2 dose strengths (see 
                        Figure A
                     ). These instructions can be used for both dose strengths.

list.item:
Do not use it if the expiration date has passed. If the expiration date has passed, safely throw away (dispose of) the carton in an FDA-cleared sharps disposal container (see 
   Step 13. Throw away (dispose of) STEQEYMA
).

Leave the prefilled syringe outside of the carton at room temperature 68°F to 77°F (20°C to 25°C) for 30 minutes to allow it to warm up (see 
                                       Figure E
                                    ).

Wash your hands with soap and water and dry them thoroughly (see 
                                       Figure F
                                    ).

Check the expiration date on the label of the prefilled syringe (see 
                                       Figure G
                                    ).

Look at the medicine and make sure that the liquid is clear to very slightly opalescent and colorless to pale yellow. (see 
                                       Figure H
                                    ).

Choose an injection site around the stomach area (abdomen), buttocks, upper legs (thighs). If a caregiver is giving the injection, the outer area of the upper arms may also be used (see 
                                       Figure I
                                    ).

Clean the skin with an alcohol wipe where you plan to give the injection (see 
                                       Figure J
                                    ).

Remove the needle cover when you are ready to inject STEQEYMA by holding the body of the prefilled syringe in one hand between the thumb and index fingers (see 
                                       Figure K
                                    ).

Hold the body of the prefilled syringe in one hand between the thumb and index fingers (see 
                                       Figure L
                                    ).

Use a quick and dart-like motion to insert the needle into the pinched skin at about a 45-degree angle (see 
                                       Figure L
                                    ).

 Inject all of the liquid by using your thumb to push the plunger all the way down (see 
                                       Figure M
                                    ).

After the prefilled syringe is empty, slowly lift your thumb from the plunger rod until the needle is completely covered by the needle safety guard (see 
                                       Figure N
                                    ).

If the needle is not covered, proceed carefully to throw away (dispose of) the syringe (see 
                                       Step 13. Throw away (dispose of) STEQEYMA
                                    ).

Some bleeding may occur. This is normal (see 
                                       Step 14. Care for the injection site
                                    ).

Put the used prefilled syringe in an FDA-cleared sharps disposal container right away after use (see 
                                       Figure O
                                    ).
